==English==

===Etymology===
US, 19th century. {{m|en|peeled|Peeled}} probably refers to keeping one's eyelids retracted.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-au-keep one's eyes peeled.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic|(with "for")}} To be [[on the alert]], to be [[watchful]].
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=1990|title=[[w:Jurassic Park|Jurassic Park]]|author=[[w:Michael Crichton|Michael Crichton]]
|passage=And directly below is our Mesozoic jungle river -- where, if you are lucky, you just may catch a glimpse of a very rare carnivore. '''Keep your eyes peeled''', everyone!}}
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|date=2003-11-14|title=Sailing into the past|author=Laura Bly|work=USA Today
|passage=lookouts posted to the port and starboard bows '''keep their eyes peeled''' for the ghostly outline of approaching traffic.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to be watchful}} {{l|en|keep an eye out}}, {{l|en|keep one's eyes open}}

